# ScrollBench Migration & Fixes

## Overview
We have successfully migrated [AsyncImageProvider](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.h#34-58) to [ScrollBench](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp#7-9), resolved deployment issues, and aligned the project structure with [SCROLLBENCH_STRATEGY.md](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/docs/SCROLLBENCH_STRATEGY.md).

## Changes

### 1. Structural Alignment (New)
- **Output Location**: Moved [ScrollBench](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp#7-9) binary output to `test_scrollbench/deploy/` to match documentation.
- **Build Script**: Updated `build.ps1` to deploy to this new location.
- **CMake**: Updated `RUNTIME_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY` to `${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/deploy`.

### 2. Unified Real Image Loading
- **AsyncImageProvider**: Integrated into ScrollBench.
- **ScrollBenchImageModel**: Updated to recursively scan directories and load real images via `AsyncImageProvider`.
- **SystemMonitor**: Added as a dependency.

### 3. Deployment Fixes
- **Missing DLLs**: Updated `build.ps1` to run `windeployqt` for `appScrollBench.exe`.

### 4. UI Adjustments
- **Thumb Resolution**: Lowered minimum resolution to **20px**.

## Verification
### functionality
- [x] **Launch**: App runs from `test_scrollbench/deploy/appScrollBench.exe`.
- [x] **Load Images**: "Select Folder" loads real images.
- [x] **Performance**: Frame Budget controls loading speed.

